t that may impair health, has been a recognized phenomenon across diverse cultures and historical periods, though its prevalence and societal perception have varied dramatically. From the opulent banquets of ancient Rome to the modern global health crisis, obesity reflects complex interactions between biology, environment, economics, and culture. Its study offers a unique lens into human dietary practices, social stratification, and the evolution of medical understanding over millennia.

